   "subject": "Re: how to adjust the distance between x ticks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hey David,<br><br>Thank you for your prompt reply.<br><br>Is there anyway that I can still show all x-ticks and just make the interval between x-ticks larger?<br><br>Thanks a lot,<br><br>Li"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\nOn Sat, Nov 28, 2009 at 11:05 AM, David Kahle <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Check out the <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">breaks <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">argument in <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">scale_x_continuous<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">, e.g.</span></span></span></span><div>\r\n<br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">qplot</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>)</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px\">qplot<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">) + </span>scale_x_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>breaks<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span>c<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">))</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">Cheers</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">david.</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:medium\"><br></span></font></div><div><div><div></div><div><div>\r\nOn Nov 28, 2009, at 10:38 AM, Li Xue wrote:</div><br></div></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div></div><div>Hello,<br><br>The labels of x ticks in my plot is too long and they overlapped. How can I make the distance between x ticks larger?<br>\r\n<br>Thanks,<br clear=\"all\"><br>Li<br><div><br></div></div></div> -- <br> You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br> To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n To unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br> For more options, visit this group at<br> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792384822315000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2vqpYEAOtuPcUHvdyryGMr\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a></blockquote>\r\n</div><br></div></div><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br>\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nFor more options, visit this group at<br>\r\n<a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gma