  {
   "id": "cXRd1dkBWGcJ",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2009-11-29T03:03:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to adjust the distance between x ticks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">You can enlarge the viewing window (either when you are viewing or saving, see ggsave() and enlarge the width).<div><br></div><div>Otherwise, if you are having a hard time reading them, say, if they overlap for example, you can try something like</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(156,34,17)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">labs</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\"> &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>&#39;Sample text&#39;<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">:</span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">10</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">qplot</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">factor</span>(<span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:#224f1e\">10</span>), <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:#224f1e\">10</span>) + </div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>scale_x_discrete<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>labels<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>labs<span style=\"color:#001b93\">) +</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>opts<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>axis.text.x<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">    </span>theme_text<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>angle<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">30</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>size<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">8</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>vjust<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">2</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>hjust<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>.75<span style=\"color:#001b93\">))</span></div></div><div><br></div><div>Hope it helps</div><div>david.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><br><div><div>On Nov 28, 2009, at 8:51 PM, Li Xue wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">Hey David,<br><br>Thank you for your prompt reply.<br><br>Is there anyway that I can still show all x-ticks and just make the interval between x-ticks larger?<br><br>Thanks a lot,<br><br>Li<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"> On Sat, Nov 28, 2009 at 11:05 AM, David Kahle <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex\"> <div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Check out the <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">breaks <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">argument in <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">scale_x_continuous<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">, e.g.</span></span></span></span><div> <br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">qplot</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>)</div> <div style=\"margin:0px\">qplot<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">) + </span>scale_x_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>breaks<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span>c<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">))</span></div> <div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">Cheers</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">david.</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:medium\"><br></span></font></div><div><div><div></div><div><div> On Nov 28, 2009, at 10:38 AM, Li Xue wrote:</div><br></div></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div></div><div>Hello,<br><br>The labels of x ticks in my plot is too long and they overlapped. How can I make the distance between x ticks larger?<br> <br>Thanks,<br clear=\"all\"><br>Li<br><div><br></div></div></div> -- <br> You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br> To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br> To unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br> For more options, visit this group at<br> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792384822317000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0K5z2-jqCovMoaxw2235Un\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a></blockquote> </div><br></div></div><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div> -- <br> You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br> To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br> To unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googl