     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Nov 28, 2009 at 9:03 PM, David Kahle <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">You can enlarge the viewing window (either when you are viewing or saving, see ggsave() and enlarge the width).<div>\r\n<br></div><div>Otherwise, if you are having a hard time reading them, say, if they overlap for example, you can try something like</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(156,34,17)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">labs</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">paste</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>&#39;Sample text&#39;<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">)</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">qplot</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">factor</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>), <span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>) + </div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  </span>scale_x_discrete<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>labels<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span>labs<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">) +</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">  </span>opts<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>axis.text.x<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">    </span>theme_text<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>angle<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">30</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span>size<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">8</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span>vjust<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span>hjust<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span>.75<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">))</span></div>\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>Hope it helps</div><div>david.</div><div><div></div><div><div><br><div><div>On Nov 28, 2009, at 8:51 PM, Li Xue wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">Hey David,<br><br>Thank you for your prompt reply.<br>\r\n<br>Is there anyway that I can still show all x-ticks and just make the interval between x-ticks larger?<br><br>Thanks a lot,<br><br>Li<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"> On Sat, Nov 28, 2009 at 11:05 AM, David Kahle <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">david...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex\"> <div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Check out the <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">breaks <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">argument in <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\">scale_x_continuous<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">, e.g.</span></span></span></span><div>\r\n <br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">qplot</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span>)</div>\r\n <div style=\"margin:0px\">qplot<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">) + </span>scale_x_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span>breaks<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\"> = </span>c<span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,79,30)\">10</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,27,147)\">))</span></div>\r\n <div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font color=\"#001b93\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">Cheers</span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px\">\r\n <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium\">david.</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px\"><font face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:medium\"><br></span></font></div><div><div><div></div><div><div> On Nov 28, 2009, at 10:38 AM, Li Xue wrote:</div>\r\n<br></div></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div></div><div>Hello,<br><br>The labels of x ticks in my plot is too long and they overlapped. How can I make the distance between x ticks larger?<br> <br>Thanks,<br clear=\"all\">\r\n<br>Li<br><div><br></div></div></div> -- <br> You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br> To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n To unsubscribe from this group, send email to<br> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br> For more options, visit this group at<br> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-sa